Subject: [PATCH] amdgpu: read-only bc250_gfx1013 marker parameter

Export a read-only module parameter that identifies this module as the
BC-250 (GFX1013) patched build, so userspace can tell a patched amdgpu
apart from a stock one.

The patched amdgpu module is installed into the image as
/usr/lib/modules/<kver>/updates/amdgpu.ko, which takes precedence over the
stock module through modules.dep. Userspace can then read

    /sys/module/amdgpu/parameters/bc250_gfx1013_v33

to confirm the running driver carries the BC-250 kernel fixes. The image's
diagnostics and driver-selection helpers use it to report which amdgpu is
live; the parameter itself changes nothing.

Adapted from the marker patch in Thunkar/bc250-bazzite-toolkit (MIT). The
upstream comment described the patch set as "compute-queue lifecycle"
patches; the vendored set here is the KFD/TTM/sclk/40CU group, so the
description is corrected.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -757,6 +757,17 @@
 	"Scheduling policy (0 = HWS (Default), 1 = HWS without over-subscription, 2 = Non-HWS (Used for debugging only)");
 
 /**
+ * DOC: bc250_gfx1013_v33 (int)
+ * Read-only marker exported by builds that carry the BC-250 (GFX1013) kernel
+ * patch set. Userspace reads /sys/module/amdgpu/parameters/bc250_gfx1013_v33
+ * to tell a patched amdgpu apart from the stock one; it selects nothing and
+ * changes no behaviour.
+ */
+int amdgpu_bc250_gfx1013_v33 = 1;
+module_param_named(bc250_gfx1013_v33, amdgpu_bc250_gfx1013_v33, int, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bc250_gfx1013_v33, "BC-250 GFX1013 kernel patch set present (read-only marker)");
+
+/**
  * DOC: hws_max_conc_proc (int)
  * Maximum number of processes that HWS can schedule concurrently. The maximum is the
  * number of VMIDs assigned to the HWS, which is also the default.
